# Colors

This system uses one neutral canvas color plus a 9-step scale for every palette.

- Left click a swatch to copy semantic token name.
- Right click for OKLCH, primitive and semantic copy options.

## Palette

<ColorGrid />

## Accent colors

Accent colors apply to interactive controls and links. Status colors do not change with the accent.

Set one of the built-in presets on the document or on a component subtree:

```html
<html data-aesir-accent="purple">
  ...
</html>
```

The available presets are `blue`, `purple`, `pink`, `orange`, `yellow`, `lime`, `green`, `teal`, and `cyan`. Red remains reserved for destructive actions and error states. See [Theming](/docs/theming/#accent-color) for custom accent values and persistence.

<ReferencePreview>
	<div class="accent-palette">
		{#each accents as accent}
			<div class="accent-sample" data-aesir-accent={accent}>
				<span class="accent-sample__swatch" aria-hidden="true"></span>
				<span>{accent}</span>
			</div>
		{/each}
	</div>
</ReferencePreview>

<DocsTable columns={accentColumns} rows={accentRows} />

## Backgrounds

- `--ds-background` is the primary app canvas.
- `--ds-background-secondary` can be used as page/section background for subtle separation.
- For tinted containers, use the `--ds-surface-*` family.

<ReferencePreview>
	<div class="background-layers">
		<div class="background-layers__secondary">
			<div class="background-layers__surface"></div>
		</div>
	</div>
</ReferencePreview>

## Scale model

<DocsTable columns={scaleColumns} rows={scaleRows} minWidth="var(--ds-sizing-2xl)" />

## Colors 100–300: surfaces

Surface steps are for component backgrounds - cards, inputs, dropdowns, panels. By default, step `1` is the resting state, `2` is hover, and `3` is active/pressed. However, this is a guideline, not a rule. If a component sits on a surface that makes step `1` hard to distinguish, start at step `2` as the default and shift hover/active up accordingly.

<DocsTable columns={stepColumns} rows={surfaceRows} />

